{
  "id": "COMPOUND:7843 - PROTEIN:1109",
  "verbalization": "Arbaclofen appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving N-sulfoglucosamine sulfohydrolase recombinant, which acts as a target for both Arbaclofen and Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf. This suggests that Arbaclofen may influence cellular processes through a common intermediate, N-sulfoglucosamine sulfohydrolase recombinant, which in turn modulates Vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 3. The evidence from the two paths indicates a potential mechanism where Arbaclofen indirectly affects Vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 3 by targeting a shared enzyme, thereby highlighting a possible role in vascular regulation. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of N-sulfoglucosamine sulfohydrolase recombinant as a central mediator in the interaction between Arbaclofen and Vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 3.",
